  "description": "TINFIG crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H120 Br8 Cl8 Eu8 N8 O36 4+,4(Cl1 1-),2(C1 H4 O1),14(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 4 O neighbors; Eu3B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4B (Eu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a chain with insufficient metal sites for a 3D shape classification. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.608-3.613 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.31-101.23°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu8L4(1,4-BDC)2Cl8(MeOH)12]·4Cl·2MeOH·18H2O (H2L = bis(5-bromo-3-methoxysalicylidene)ethylene-1,2-phenylenediamine; 1,4-H2BDC = 1,4-benzenedicarboxylic acid).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
